  {
    "id": "2104662741092897266",
    "author": "MattRobbt",
    "name": "Matt Robb",
    "text": "So things have blown up around my interaction with Muse with the whole Facebook buyer showing up at my door.\nBut this tool is public and free. I'm glad it happened to me and not someone more vulnerable tbh. Imagine some old lady in a house with a random guy banging on her door angry at 10pm. I'm just saying the average user will prompt worse than a tech guy (have you seen Facebook comments these days). Just the other day someone on my Threads feed posted a photo of their passport. No hate to meta I love tech and I'm not an anti AI person at all. But yeah it's getting intrusive for sure. \n\nWe definitely need clearer signals when an AI is talking on someone's behalf (it should have a \"Sent by Muse\" tag), and much tighter restrictions on sensitive info.",
